  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas undergoes&nbsp;the cyclic process <math> <mrow> <mtext>abca</mtext></mrow> </math>as shown in the figure. The&nbsp;internal energy change of the gas along the path <math> <mrow> <mtext>c</mtext><mtext>a</mtext></mrow> </math> &nbsp;is&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>J</mtext></mrow> </math>. The gas absorb <math> <mrow> <mn>250</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>J</mtext></mrow> </math> of heat along the path <math> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext><mtext>b</mtext></mrow> </math> &nbsp;and also absorbs&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>J</mtext></mrow> </math> &nbsp;of heat along&nbsp;the path <math> <mrow> <mtext>bc</mtext></mrow> </math>. Find the work done by the gas along the path <math> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext><mtext>b</mtext><mtext>c</mtext></mrow></math><br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0156_5badc23dc323.jpeg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 190px;\" />"
  },
